# .semgrepignore (P29a step 7) - traversal pruning for the pinned semgrep image.
#
# There is no .gitignore-driven pruning here (this repo has no git, ADR 0003),
# so without this file semgrep WALKS every node_modules / dist / build tree
# before applying the CLI --exclude patterns - on the Windows Docker Desktop
# bind mount that walk alone took ~16 minutes on 2026-09-09. Directories
# listed here are pruned during targeting and never entered.
#
# This file only narrows WHERE semgrep looks; the rules live in .semgrep.yml
# and the per-rule test/fixture exclusions live there and in the CLI flags
# (scripts/guards/security-scan-lib.ts). Keep the three lists in agreement.
#
# scripts/guards/__fixtures__/ is deliberately NOT listed: the fixture proof
# (`each_scanner_fails_on_its_seeded_fixture`) points semgrep AT that tree, and
# an ignore here would prune the scan target itself and turn the proof into a
# silent zero-file pass (P29a C1 CRITICAL, 2026-09-09). The repo-root scan
# excludes it through the CLI --exclude flags instead.
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.turbo/
.next/
website/out/
demo/
.memory/
.claude/
.secrets/
.data/
test-results/
